ull,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2025-12-10T12:13:42Z","updated_at":"2025-12-11T09:49:44Z","closed_at":"2025-12-11T09:42:53Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Tested and reproduced in in **Godot v4.4.1.stable** and **Godot v4.5.1.stable**\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS 24.04 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Mobile) - integrated Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics (ADL GT2) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-1255U (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nCustom/user-defined monitors under the debugger tab can be selected to be visualized. However, when you run the project, the custom monitors are reset to be unselected, while the built-in monitors remain unchanged. The visualization is also hidden, suggesting that this issue goes beyond the state of the checkbox state in UI.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- In any project, including a new empty one, make sure that `Performance.add_custom_monitor` is run at least once in your project. This should register a new monitor that will be remembered by the editor _session until you close it_.\n- Go to Debugger > Monitors and scroll down to the new custom monitor, typically located at the bottom. Select this monitor for visualization, as well as at least one built-in monitor.\n- Run the project, and return to the monitor window, and compare the selection state of the monitors to before you ran the project\n\nEDIT: specified that the monitor is only remembered until the editor is closed. Thanks to @arkology for pointing it out!\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[custom_monitor_mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24077023/custom_monitor_mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"automathan","id":13404443,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNDA0NDQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13404443?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/automathan","html_url":"https://github.com/automathan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automathan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automathan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automathan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automathan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automathan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automathan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automathan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automathan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/automathan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113840/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113840/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}